# 124 - §6 (.37): re-declaring a name in the SAME scope is LEGAL, not an
# error, and the later `let` wins. Each initialiser still sees the binding that
# was current before its own `let`, so this is 1 -> 2 -> 20. An engine that
# rejected the redeclaration, or that resolved all three lets to one slot
# before running them, gets a different answer.
--- source
let x = 1;
let x = x + 1;
let x = x * 10;
print x;
--- expect
20
